<!--Post: 4238--><!--Time: 1105937325-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4238"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Pax56<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Pax56<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, January 16, 2005 - 8:48 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I don&#39;t want to start a blame-throwing match here, just some reasoned debate.  One my KU sources reported seeing this article in the Lawrence paper: <BR> <BR><a href="http://ljworld.com/section/stateregional/story/193233" target=_top>http://ljworld.com/section/stateregional/story/193 233</a> <BR> <BR>Looks like this one would be a hot potato for the local media.  I hate to side with either the police or the media.  I think the media have a justifiable hunger to see this end.  But at the same time, I want the police to succeed.  I&#39;m worried that media actions could jeopardize things, particularly if BTK is getting some lucky breaks. <BR> <BR>Who&#39;s right here?  Opinions welcome!  -pax<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4238-->
<!--Post: 4239--><!--Time: 1105941409-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4239"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, January 16, 2005 - 9:56 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Thanks, Pax for an important thread. Before I start, did you see the story, extending from above link, where someone torched a funeral home wherein three bodies which had been prepared for viewing were burned? Unrelated but so unusual. <BR> <BR>I side a bit more with WPD. If WPD say they need a little breathing room to do their jobs, that should come first. If the Feds really are going to use $15 million in an effort to capture BTK, then it may be a moot point. But for now, WPD.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4239-->
<!--Post: 4242--><!--Time: 1105942412-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4242"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Angrywolf<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Angrywolf<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, January 16, 2005 - 10:13 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->my view is the WPD was incompetent to arrest Valdez without more evidence and are blaming the media to cover their mistakes....I hope Valdez takes all of them to the cleaners though like Richard Jewel did down in Georgia...<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4242-->
<!--Post: 4246--><!--Time: 1105960157-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4246"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Researcher<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Researcher<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, January 17, 2005 - 3:09 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Well it will be interesting to see who the tip came from and why.  Hopefully the civil trial, if not settled out of court, will yield those answers.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4246-->
<!--Post: 4253--><!--Time: 1105975379-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4253"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Beck<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Beck<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, January 17, 2005 - 7:22 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->It&#39;s hard to side with the WPD when you look at how they have handled this case.  <BR> <BR>Roger Valdez- that could have been handled WAY better than it was. The above link to the news story said that Valdez had warrants on him. Why not take him in for whatever those warrants were for, and then ask questions to find out for sure if he could have been BTK? Not to mention, they had no warrant to use obtain a DNA sample without him permission.  <BR> <BR>Why didn&#39;t they tell Charlie Otero about BTK? Apparently he didn&#39;t find out about it until a lawyer told him 1994. I personally believe that he could help a lot with this case.  <BR> <BR>I&#39;m all for police keeping some things secret, so that they can tell when a communication is actually coming from the suspect, but there is so much that could be released to the public that may actually help lead to an arrest! <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4253-->
<!--Post: 4287--><!--Time: 1106042253-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4287"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, January 18, 2005 - 1:57 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->The 1970s press didn&#39;t do a wonderful job with the case, either.  <BR> <BR>To the topic, where is the information that the Feds are going to be pouring millions of dollars into the BTK hunt? I kept hearing this a week ago yet see no signs of it. It&#39;ll change everything if true.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4287-->
<!--Post: 4294--><!--Time: 1106054201-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4294"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Flytodeb<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Flytodeb<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->6-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, January 18, 2005 - 5:16 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->George, the federal money is to pay for DNA testing. $15 thousand, not millions. Sorry to say so.  <BR>-Deb <BR> <BR><a href="http://www.kake.com/news/headlines/1142762.html" target=_top>http://www.kake.com/news/headlines/1142762.html</a><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4294-->
<!--Post: 4316--><!--Time: 1106143363-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4316"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, January 19, 2005 - 6:02 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Deb: <i>Sorry to say so.</i>  <BR> <BR>That I doubt but thanks for the clarification. I&#39;ve repeatedly read this figure, 15 mllion, by a couple of Kansans who were obviously wrong. Salient point is that 15K means squat. The Feds consider the case hopeless; if not, they&#39;d be in Wichita in full force. In light of this 15K information, BTK isn&#39;t going to be caught.  I hope that at least his name will be learned. Then again, he may drive 1,500 miles away, destroy his car, then jump off a cliff, with no ID, and never be known. <BR> <BR>Angrywolf, I now agree completely with your point of view.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4316-->
<!--Post: 4366--><!--Time: 1106245876-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4366"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Jim44095<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Jim44095<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, January 20, 2005 - 10:31 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->It would be interesting to know just how many cases have been solved by media attention and information given out.If the media is not any help then why has John Walsh&#39; program lasted so long?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4366-->
<!--Post: 4367--><!--Time: 1106246183-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4367"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Jim44095<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Jim44095<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, January 20, 2005 - 10:36 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->George I too found that funeral home story odd,it occured on the 15th,although fire has not been his m-o there is a body that has not been identified yet,as of the article.Who could possibly want to tourch a funeral home?that&#39;s just creepy.Can&#39;t remmeber did the owner live there?If not what is the point?Unless you&#39;re a pyro.lol<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4367-->
<!--Post: 4378--><!--Time: 1106266001-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4378"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Tornado<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tornado<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, January 20, 2005 - 4:06 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Rumor has it that the torching of the funeral home was in regards to a shooting victim whose body was in the funeral home at the time of the burning.  It has been said that it is gang related.  <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4378-->
